{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>All the soul coming to Jacob.</b> Even though they were many souls, Scripture nevertheless calls them all 'soul' (נֶפֶשׁ, singular), because before this the brothers were jealous of Joseph and they were divided souls, but now they had become as one and their jealousy had ceased, and Joseph too bore no grudge against them. Therefore Scripture informs us that they were all one soul, to testify to the righteousness of Joseph and to the righteousness of the brothers. Accordingly it first said, ״כָּל הַנֶּפֶשׁ הַבָּאָה לְבֵית יַעֲקֹב מִצְרַיְמָה״ (Genesis 46:26), to testify to the righteousness of the brothers, and afterward it returned and said, ״וּבְנֵי יוֹסֵף וְגוֹ׳ כָּל הַנֶּפֶשׁ לְבֵית יַעֲקֹב הַבָּאָה מִצְרַיְמָה שִׁבְעִים״ (Genesis 46:27), to testify to the righteousness of Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:37.383177212Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}